<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Design Document</title></head><body><div style="font-family: Segoe UI, Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; color: #ffffff; background-color: #1a1a2e; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px;"><h1 style="color: #60a5fa; border-bottom: 3px solid #60a5fa; padding-bottom: 10px; margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 28px;">Design Document</h1><p style="color: #cbd5e1; font-style: italic; margin-bottom: 20px; font-size: 14px;">Generated by Mistral Small on 9/16/2026, 10:05:35 AM | Session: 3c17b3c9...</p><div style="margin-bottom: 32px; border-left: 3px solid #f97316; padding-left: 16px;"><h2 style="color: #f97316; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 18px;">1. Architecture Overview</h2><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**Architecture Overview**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**1. Introduction**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">This Architecture Overview lays the foundation for the AI-Driven Banking Contract Retrieval with Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) project. The objective is to develop a secure, efficient, and customer-friendly solution that enables bank customers to access their contract information through a conversational service channel.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**2. Design Philosophy**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The design philosophy for this solution is based on a microservices architecture, enabling scalability, modularity, and independent development, testing, and deployment of services. This approach promotes a loosely coupled system, which enhances fault tolerance and facilitates the integration of third-party services as required.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**3. System Architecture**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The system architecture consists of several interconnected components, as illustrated in Figure 1 below.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">```</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">+-------------------+               +-------------------+</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">|    Customer UI    |               |     Authentication |</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">+-------------------+               +-------------------+</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">|                   |               |                   |</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">|  Conversational AI |               | Authentication   |</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">|                   |               |  Service (AuthN)   |</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">|                   |               |                   |</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">|                   |               +-------------------+</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">|                   |                           |</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">|+------------------+---------------------------+</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">||                      |                            |</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">||   Summarization     |           Audit Logging     |</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">||  Service (Summarize)|                            |</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">||                      |                            |</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">|+------------------+---------------------------+</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">|                      |</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">|    Contract Data   |</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">|                      |</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">|+------------------+</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">||                      |</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">||     Contract DB     |</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">||                      |</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">+</p></div><div style="margin-bottom: 32px; border-left: 3px solid #f97316; padding-left: 16px;"><h2 style="color: #f97316; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 18px;">2. Component Design</h2><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**Component Design**</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Customer Authentication and Verification Component (CAVC)**</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The CAVC is responsible for verifying the identity of the bank customers who initiate contract information requests. This component will utilize a multi-factor authentication system, combining elements such as passwords, one-time passcodes (OTPs), biometrics, and device recognition to ensure a high level of security.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Responsibilities:</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Authenticating and verifying user identity</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Ensuring secure storage and transmission of authentication data</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Detecting and preventing unauthorized access attempts</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Boundaries:</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">The component will primarily interact with the User Interface (UI) component to receive user credentials and return authentication status.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">The CAVC will also communicate with the Customer Database to verify user credentials and verify the customer's eligibility to access contract information.</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Inter-Component Communication:</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The CAVC will use secure, encrypted APIs to communicate with the UI and Customer Database components.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Lifecycle and Deployment Considerations:</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">The CAVC will be deployed as a microservice, allowing for scalability and high availability.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">The component will be configured to implement appropriate security measures, such as rate limiting, IP whitelisting, and intrusion detection systems.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Natural Language Processing (NLP) Component**</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The NLP component will enable the conversational interface by understanding and interpreting the user's requests regarding contract information.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Responsibilities:</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Parsing user input to extract relevant information</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Identifying the type of contract information being requested</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Generating structured queries for the Contract Retrieval component</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Boundaries:</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">The NLP component will primarily interact with the UI component to receive user input and provide response options.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">The NLP component will also communicate with the Contract</li></div><div style="margin-bottom: 32px; border-left: 3px solid #f97316; padding-left: 16px;"><h2 style="color: #f97316; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 18px;">3. Data Models</h2><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**Data Models Section**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">In this section, we will define the primary data entities and their relationships, describe data schemas for each entity, explain data consistency and integrity constraints, address data lifecycle management, discuss indexing and query optimization strategies, and include ER diagrams or data relationship descriptions to support the architecture and components defined in the project specification.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**1. Customer Entity**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The Customer entity represents the individuals or entities interacting with the system. It stores customer-specific information for identification, authentication, and authorization purposes.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">CustomerID (Primary Key, String, 36 characters, UUID)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">FirstName (String, 50 characters)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">LastName (String, 50 characters)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Email (String, 254 characters)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">PhoneNumber (String, 20 characters)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">DateOfBirth (Date)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">NationalID (String, 15 characters)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">AccountNumber (String, 20 characters)</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**2. Contract Entity**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The Contract entity stores the details of the agreements between the bank and the customers.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">ContractID (Primary Key, String, 36 characters, UUID)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">CustomerID (Foreign Key, String, 36 characters, UUID)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">ContractType (Enum: Loan, Mortgage, CreditCard, SavingsAccount, etc.)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">ContractStatus (Enum: Active, Inactive, Terminated, etc.)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">EffectiveDate (Date)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">ExpirationDate (Date)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">InterestRate (Decimal)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">LateFee (Decimal)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">EarlyRepaymentFee (Decimal)</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**3. ContractSummary Entity**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The ContractSummary entity stores concise summaries of contract content to provide customers with quick access to key information.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">SummaryID (Primary Key,</li></div><div style="margin-bottom: 32px; border-left: 3px solid #f97316; padding-left: 16px;"><h2 style="color: #f97316; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 18px;">4. Interface Definitions</h2><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**Interface Definitions**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**1. API Definitions**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**1.1 Customer Authentication API**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The Customer Authentication API (CAAPI) is responsible for authenticating customers before granting access to their contract information. It uses OAuth 2.0 for secure authorization.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**Request**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">```json</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">{</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">"username": "&lt;customer_username&gt;",</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">"password": "&lt;customer_password&gt;"</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">}</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">```</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**Response**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">```json</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">{</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">"access_token": "&lt;access_token&gt;",</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">"token_type": "Bearer",</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">"expires_in": &lt;expiration_time_in_seconds&gt;,</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">"refresh_token": "&lt;refresh_token&gt;"</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">}</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">```</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**1.2 Contract Retrieval API**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The Contract Retrieval API (CRAPI) retrieves contract information for authenticated customers. It uses JSON Web Tokens (JWT) for authorization.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**Request**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">```json</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">{</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">"contract_id": "&lt;contract_id&gt;"</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">}</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">```</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**Response**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">```json</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">{</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">"contract": {</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">"id": "&lt;contract_id&gt;",</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">"customer_id": "&lt;customer_id&gt;",</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">"summary": "&lt;contract_summary&gt;",</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">"full_content": "&lt;contract_full_content&gt;"</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">}</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">}</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">```</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**1.3 Contract Summary Generation API**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The Contract Summary Generation API (CSGAPI) generates a concise summary of the contract content. It uses JWT for authorization.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**Request**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">```json</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">{</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">"contract_content": "&lt;contract_full_content&gt;"</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">}</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">```</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**Response**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">```json</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">{</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">"summary</p></div><div style="margin-bottom: 32px; border-left: 3px solid #f97316; padding-left: 16px;"><h2 style="color: #f97316; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 18px;">5. API Specifications</h2><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**API Specifications**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**1. API Overview**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The AI-Driven Banking Contract Retrieval API is a RESTful API that facilitates secure and efficient access to contract-related information for authenticated bank customers. The API utilizes natural language processing (NLP) to understand user queries and delivers concise, understandable responses.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**2. API Endpoints**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**2.1 Authentication (POST /auth)**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">This endpoint is used to authenticate the user. The request should include a JSON body with the user's credentials.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**Request**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">```json</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">{</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">"username": "john.doe",</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">"password": "password123"</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">}</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">```</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**Response**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Upon successful authentication, a JSON Web Token (JWT) is returned.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">```json</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">{</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">"token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJ1c2VyX2lkIjoxMjMsInVzZXJuYW1lIjoidGVzdF91c2VyIn0.q29udHJ1c3Rlcm1zaXZlX2lkIn0."</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">}</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">```</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">If the credentials are incorrect, an HTTP 401 Unauthorized status is returned.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**2.2 Contract Information (GET /contracts)**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">This endpoint is used to retrieve contract information for the authenticated user. The request should include the JWT token received during authentication.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**Request**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">```json</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">{</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">"authorization": "Bearer eyJhbGciO</p></div><div style="margin-bottom: 32px; border-left: 3px solid #f97316; padding-left: 16px;"><h2 style="color: #f97316; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 18px;">6. Security Architecture</h2><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**Security Architecture**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">In this AI-Driven Banking Contract Retrieval with Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) project, a secure and compliant architecture is crucial to protect sensitive customer data and maintain trust. This section outlines the security measures and controls to address the specified requirements and mitigate potential threats.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Authentication and Authorization Strategy**</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">To ensure that only authenticated customers can access their contract information, the system will implement OAuth 2.0 for secure user authentication and authorization. This protocol allows for user consent, delegation, and revocation of access.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Additionally, JSON Web Tokens (JWT) will be utilized for efficient and secure transmission of user identity, allowing the system to identify authenticated users and their authorized actions.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) will be employed to manage user roles, permissions, and access levels based on their job functions and responsibilities within the banking organization.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Encryption Requirements**</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">All communication between the user and the system will be encrypted using Transport Layer Security (TLS) to protect data in transit. At-rest encryption will be implemented using AES-256 to protect data that is stored on the system.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Secrets Management and Credential Handling**</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">To manage secrets and protect sensitive data, a centralized secrets management system will be implemented. This system will securely store and manage encryption keys, certificates, and other sensitive information.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Access to the secrets management system will be tightly controlled using RBAC and multi-factor authentication (MFA) to prevent unauthorized access.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Audit Logging and Compliance Requirements**</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The system will maintain a comprehensive audit trail of all user interactions, including request and response details</p></div><div style="margin-bottom: 32px; border-left: 3px solid #f97316; padding-left: 16px;"><h2 style="color: #f97316; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 18px;">7. Performance Considerations</h2><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Performance Considerations Section</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Performance Targets</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">To ensure an optimal user experience, the following performance targets have been established for the AI-Driven Banking Contract Retrieval system with Human-in-the-Loop (HITL).</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Latency: The system should aim to respond to user requests within 3 seconds, with a 95th percentile response time of 5 seconds or less. This includes the time taken for request processing, contract information retrieval, and response formatting.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Throughput: The system should be capable of handling at least 10,000 requests per minute during peak hours, with a graceful degradation of performance beyond this threshold. This will allow for efficient handling of high volumes of user requests while maintaining performance targets.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Concurrency: The system should support concurrent requests from multiple users without causing significant impact on response times or system stability. To achieve this, the system should be designed to manage and prioritize requests effectively, ensuring that critical operations are not affected by high concurrency levels.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Caching Strategy and Invalidation</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">To improve system performance and reduce database load, a caching strategy will be employed. Both in-memory and distributed caching solutions may be considered. Commonly cached items will include contract summaries, user authentication data, and frequently requested contract information.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Cached items will be invalidated based on predefined expiration policies, as well as when relevant data changes occur. Changes to contract information, user authentication status, or other critical data will trigger cache invalidation to ensure that the system always serves up-to-date information.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Database Query Optimization and Indexing</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">To minimize the impact of database operations on system performance, extensive efforts will be made to optimize database queries and properly index database tables. This will include query refactoring, index creation,</p></div><div style="margin-bottom: 32px; border-left: 3px solid #f97316; padding-left: 16px;"><h2 style="color: #f97316; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 18px;">8. Error Handling Strategy</h2><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Error Handling Strategy</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">In the AI-Driven Banking Contract Retrieval with Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) project, a robust and comprehensive error handling strategy is essential to ensure system resilience, maintain high customer satisfaction, and adhere to regulatory requirements. This section outlines the approach for defining an error classification system, retry logic, circuit breaker pattern, error logging and monitoring, graceful degradation strategies, user-facing error messages, and recovery suggestions.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Error Classification System</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The error handling strategy will classify errors into two categories: retriable and non-retriable. Retriable errors are temporary issues that can be resolved by retrying the operation after a delay. Non-retriable errors are permanent or critical issues that require immediate attention and cannot be resolved by retries.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Retriable errors may include network errors, timeouts, or transient database issues. Non-retriable errors may include system failures, data inconsistencies, or security breaches.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Retry Logic with Exponential Backoff</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">For retriable errors, the system will implement retry logic with exponential backoff. This means that if an error occurs, the system will wait an increasing amount of time before attempting to retry the operation. The initial retry delay will be set to a short duration, and the delay will be doubled for each subsequent retry up to a maximum limit. This approach reduces the number of retries and minimizes the impact on system performance.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Circuit Breaker Pattern</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">To prevent cascading failures and protect the overall system from the impact of intermittent issues, the system will implement the circuit breaker pattern. When a certain number of retriable errors occur within a specific time frame, the circuit breaker will trip, and the system will transition to an open state. In</p></div><div style="margin-bottom: 32px; border-left: 3px solid #f97316; padding-left: 16px;"><h2 style="color: #f97316; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 18px;">9. Logging and Monitoring</h2><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**Logging and Monitoring Strategy**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The AI-Driven Banking Contract Retrieval with Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) solution will employ a robust logging and monitoring strategy to ensure the system's availability, reliability, security, and compliance. This section outlines the logging levels, structured logging format, metrics collection, alerting strategy, log aggregation, distributed tracing, and dashboard requirements.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Logging Levels and Structured Logging Format**</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The logging levels will be defined as follows:</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Emergency (EMERGENCY)**: System is unusable.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Alert (ALERT)**: Immediate action is needed.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Critical (CRITICAL)**: System is severely compromised or service is unavailable.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Error (ERROR)**: Runtime errors that prevent normal operation.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Warning (WARNING)**: Potential issues that could lead to errors if not addressed.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Notice (NOTICE)**: Informational messages that provide insight into the system's behavior.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Debug (DEBUG)**: Detailed trace information useful for debugging.</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Structured logs will be used to ensure consistency, ease parsing, and enable efficient analysis. Each log entry will include a timestamp, log level, component/service, request/response ID, user ID (if applicable), error code (if applicable), and a detailed message.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Metrics Collection**</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Metrics will be collected for CPU, memory, latency, and error rates to monitor system performance and identify potential bottlenecks or issues.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**CPU and Memory**: Resource usage will be monitored to ensure the system can handle the expected load and identify potential performance issues.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Latency**: Response times at various points in the system will be measured to ensure acceptable performance for users</li></div><div style="margin-bottom: 32px; border-left: 3px solid #f97316; padding-left: 16px;"><h2 style="color: #f97316; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 18px;">10. Deployment Architecture</h2><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**Deployment Architecture**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The following deployment architecture is proposed for the AI-Driven Banking Contract Retrieval with Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) project. This architecture ensures high availability, scalability, security, and compliance, while providing a reliable and efficient service to end-users.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**1. Deployment Topology**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The deployment will be divided into multiple regions based on the bank's geographical presence to reduce latency and ensure data residency. Each region will consist of multiple availability zones to provide fault tolerance and disaster recovery capabilities.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**1.1 Regions and Availability Zones**</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Region A1 (North America East)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Availability Zone A1a</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Availability Zone A1b</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Availability Zone A1c</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Region E1 (Europe West)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Availability Zone E1a</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Availability Zone E1b</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Availability Zone E1c</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Region AP1 (Asia Pacific)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Availability Zone AP1a</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Availability Zone AP1b</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Availability Zone AP1c</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**1.2 Pods and Instances**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Within each availability zone, pods will be used to ensure application scalability and high availability. Each pod will consist of multiple instances to provide horizontal scaling and failover capabilities.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Frontend pod (Web servers)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Backend pod (API servers, AI services)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Database pod (Read replicas)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Database master pod (Primary database)</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Worker pod (Human-in-the-loop services)</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**2. Infrastructure-as-Code Approach**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Infrastructure will be managed using Terraform, an open-source infrastructure as code software. The code will be version-controlled using</p></div><div style="margin-bottom: 32px; border-left: 3px solid #f97316; padding-left: 16px;"><h2 style="color: #f97316; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 18px;">11. Development Workflow</h2><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**Development Workflow**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The following development workflow is designed to facilitate the efficient and secure development, testing, and deployment of the AI-Driven Banking Contract Retrieval with Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) system.</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**1. Local Development Environment Setup**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">To set up the local development environment, follow these steps:</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Install Node.js (LTS version): https://nodejs.org/en/download/</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Install Yarn package manager: https://yarnpkg.com/lang/en/docs/install/</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Clone the project repository from GitHub: `git clone &lt;repository_url&gt;`</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">Navigate to the project directory and install dependencies: `yarn install`</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**2. Code Organization and Module Structure**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The project will follow the Modular Monolith architecture, with a clear separation of concerns. The main modules are:</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">`api`: Contains the Express.js server and API endpoints</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">`bot`: Contains the Dialogflow integration and the AI-driven conversation logic</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">`auth`: Handles user authentication and authorization</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">`contracts`: Manages contract data storage and retrieval</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">`summarizer`: Generates summaries of contract content</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">`audit`: Records relevant activities for auditing and compliance purposes</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">`human-interaction`: Interface for escalating complex or sensitive cases to a human representative</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**3. Git Workflow**</p><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Our Git workflow consists of the following branches:</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">`main`: The production branch containing only merged, tested, and stable code.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">`develop`: The primary development branch where new features, bug fixes, and improvements are implemented.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">`feature/&lt;issue_number&gt;`: Branches for implementing</li></div><div style="margin-bottom: 32px; border-left: 3px solid #f97316; padding-left: 16px;"><h2 style="color: #f97316; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 18px;">12. Testing Strategy</h2><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**Testing Strategy**</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Test Pyramid**</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The testing strategy for the AI-Driven Banking Contract Retrieval with Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) system will adhere to a well-structured test pyramid to ensure optimal test coverage and efficiency. The pyramid will consist of three layers:</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Unit Tests (~80%):** These tests will be focused on individual units or components within the system, such as functions, methods, and classes. Unit tests will verify the functionality, behavior, and interactions of each component in isolation. This layer forms the foundation of the pyramid and ensures that the system's building blocks are error-free and reliable.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Integration Tests (~10%):** These tests will focus on the integration of multiple components or modules within the system. Integration tests will verify that the components work together seamlessly, handle data exchange, and adhere to defined interfaces. This layer bridges the gap between the unit tests and end-to-end tests.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**End-to-End Tests (~5%):** These tests will simulate the system's interactions from the user's perspective, ensuring that the entire system functions correctly and delivers the expected user experience. End-to-end tests will validate the system's flow, performance, and usability.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Testing Tools and Frameworks**</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">To ensure efficient and effective testing, the following tools and frameworks will be utilized:</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Unit Testing Framework:** JUnit for Java-based components and Mocha for JavaScript-based components.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Integration Testing Framework:** TestNG for Java-based components and Mocha for JavaScript-based components.</li><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**End-to-End Testing Frame</li></div><div style="margin-bottom: 32px; border-left: 3px solid #f97316; padding-left: 16px;"><h2 style="color: #f97316; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 18px;">13. Documentation Guidelines</h2><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">**Documentation Guidelines for AI-Driven Banking Contract Retrieval with Human-in-the-Loop (HITL)**</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Documentation Structure and Organization**</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">All documentation should be structured in a clear and organized manner to ensure easy navigation and understanding. The main sections should include: Introduction, System Overview, Architecture, API Documentation, User Guide, Runbook, Troubleshooting Guide, Architecture Decision Records (ADRs), Maintenance and Updates, Knowledge Transfer, and Training Materials.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**API Documentation Standards**</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">API documentation should adhere to industry standards such as the OpenAPI Specification (formerly Swagger) or RAML. Each API endpoint should have a clear description, input parameters, expected responses, and error handling details. The documentation should also include examples of request and response formats.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Runbook and Troubleshooting Guide Requirements**</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">A runbook should be created to outline the steps for common and complex tasks, including system setup, configuration, and maintenance. It should also provide troubleshooting procedures for common issues. The runbook should be living document, updated as the system evolves.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Architecture Decision Record (ADR) Process**</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">The ADR process should be documented, detailing the steps for proposing, evaluating, documenting, and approving architecture decisions. Each ADR should include the problem to be solved, proposed solution, alternatives considered, benefits and drawbacks, and decision rationale.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Maintenance and Update Procedures**</li><p style="margin: 10px 0; line-height: 1.8; text-align: justify; color: #e2e8f0;">Documentation should detail the procedures for system maintenance, updates, and upgrades. This should include procedures for testing updates, rollback procedures, and communication procedures for notifying stakeholders.</p><li style="margin: 6px 0; line-height: 1.6; margin-left: 20px; color: #f1f5f9;">**Knowledge Transfer and Training</li></div></div></body></html>